                        "entry_id": "3b02a503-874a-3479-bc97-63868f1c82ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to the hydrolysis of starch."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d356eca-ec92-451f-b889-390b2a1d35a9",
                                "sense_id": "45490649-739c-3409-93f1-5fd096974721",
                                "text": "Young germinating plants are able to liquefy and assimilate starch. [...] Observations on germinating maize showed that the whole plant, with the exception of the root, excreted an amylohydrolytic enzyme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a9590db-907d-4262-a30a-d02cb6e27b35",
                                "sense_id": "45490649-739c-3409-93f1-5fd096974721",
                                "text": "Brown and Escombe subjected the work of Brown and Morris to a re-investigation which resulted in a demonstration of both a cytohydrolytic and an amylohydrolytic capacity in the aleurone cells of barley. They were, however, unable to demonstrate an amylohydrolytic capacity for the amyliferous cells."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5d1d9d4-eeb1-4cca-9a85-ae99d7a6cabc",
                                "sense_id": "45490649-739c-3409-93f1-5fd096974721",
                                "text": "However, only comparative studies of proteolytic and amylohydrolytic digestive activities may reveal the ability of fish to use carbohydrates and the many sources of proteins."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
